e x-coordinate is:\n\nx = cos \u03b8 (a + (a/(a + b ))(b - a )) = cos \u03b8 [ a + (a(b - a ))/(a + b ) ]\n\n= cos \u03b8 [ (a(a + b ) + a(b - a )) / (a + b ) ]\n\n= cos \u03b8 [ (a\u00b2 + a b + a b - a\u00b2 ) / (a + b ) ]\n\n= cos \u03b8 [ 2ab / (a + b ) ]\n\nBut this x-coordinate must equal p, since point P is (p, 0). Therefore,\n\np = (2ab cos \u03b8 ) / (a + b )\n\nSimilarly, for line CD passing through P(p, 0), with C on OX and D on OY, we have:\n\np = (2cd cos \u03b8 ) / (c + d )\n\nTherefore, for both lines AB and CD, we have:\n\n2ab cos \u03b8 / (a + b ) = p\n\n2cd cos \u03b8 / (c + d ) = p\n\nTherefore, these relations hold for both lines. So from these, we can express a in terms of b and p, and c in terms of d and p:\n\nFrom 2ab cos \u03b8 = p(a + b )\n\n=> 2ab cos \u03b8 - p a - p b = 0\n\n=> a(2b cos \u03b8 - p ) = p b\n\n=> a = (p b ) / (2b cos \u03b8 - p )\n\nSimilarly,\n\nc = (p d ) / (2d cos \u03b8 - p )\n\nNow, let's compute the products OC\u00b7OA\u00b7BD and OB\u00b7OD\u00b7AC.\n\nFirst, OA is the distance from O to A, which is sqrt( (a cos \u03b8 )\u00b2 + (a sin \u03b8 )\u00b2 ) = a sqrt( cos\u00b2 \u03b8 + sin\u00b2 \u03b8 ) = a.\n\nSimilarly, OB = b, OC = c, OD = d.\n\nBD is the distance between B and D. Point B is (b cos \u03b8, -b sin \u03b8 ), point D is (d cos \u03b8, -d sin \u03b8 ).\n\nSo BD = sqrt( (d cos \u03b8 - b cos \u03b8 )\u00b2 + ( -d sin \u03b8 + b sin \u03b8 )\u00b2 )\n\n= sqrt( cos\u00b2 \u03b8 (d - b )\u00b2 + sin\u00b2 \u03b8 (b - d )\u00b2 )\n\n= |d - b | sqrt( cos\u00b2 \u03b8 + sin\u00b2 \u03b8 )\n\n= |d - b |.\n\nSimilarly, AC is the distance between A(a cos \u03b8, a sin \u03b8 ) and C(c cos \u03b8, c sin \u03b8 ):\n\nAC = sqrt( (c cos \u03b8 - a cos \u03b8 )\u00b2 + (c sin \u03b8 - a sin \u03b8 )\u00b2 )\n\n= sqrt( cos\u00b2 \u03b8 (c - a )\u00b2 + sin\u00b2 \u03b8 (c - a )\u00b2 )\n\n= |c - a | sqrt( cos\u00b2 \u03b8 + sin\u00b2 \u03b8 )\n\n= |c - a |.\n\nTherefore, OC\u00b7OA\u00b7BD = c * a * |d - b |\n\nOB\u00b7OD\u00b7AC = b * d * |c - a |\n\nSo the equation to prove is:\n\nc a |d - b | = b d |c - a |.\n\nSince all quantities a, b, c, d are positive (they are distances along the rays from O), we can drop the absolute value signs if we can determine the sign of (d - b ) and (c - a ). However, depending on the positions of the points, d could be greater or less than b, and c greater or less than a.\n\nBut from the earlier expressions:\n\na = (p b ) / (2b cos \u03b8 - p )\n\nSince a must be positive, the denominator must be positive:\n\n2b cos \u03b8 - p > 0 => b > p / (2 cos \u03b8 )\n\nSimilarly, for c:\n\n2d cos \u03b8 - p > 0 => d > p / (2 cos \u03b8 )\n\nTherefore, both b and d are greater than p / (2 cos \u03b8 ). However, the relative sizes of b and d are not fixed. Similarly, a and c depend on b and d.\n\nBut let's proceed with the expressions.\n\nGiven a = (p b ) / (2b cos \u03b8 - p )\n\nSimilarly, c = (p d ) / (2d cos \u03b8 - p )\n\nLet\u2019s compute c - a:\n\nc - a = (p d)/(2d cos \u03b8 - p ) - (p b )/(2b cos \u03b8 - p )\n\nLet me find a common denominator:\n\n= [ p d (2b cos \u03b8 - p ) - p b (2d cos \u03b8 - p ) ] / [ (2d cos \u03b8 - p )(2b cos \u03b8 - p ) ]\n\nFactor p:\n\n= p [ d (2b cos \u03b8 - p ) - b (2d cos \u03b8 - p ) ] / [ (2d cos \u03b8 - p )(2b cos \u03b8 - p ) ]\n\nExpand inside the brackets:\n\n= p [ 2b d cos \u03b8 - d p - 2b d cos \u03b8 + b p ] / denominator\n\nSimplify:\n\n= p [ -d p + b p ] / denominator\n\n= p [ p (b - d ) ] / denominator\n\n= p\u00b2 (b - d ) / [ (2d cos \u03b8 - p )(2b cos \u03b8 - p ) ]\n\nTherefore,\n\nc - a = p\u00b2 (b - d ) / [ (2d cos \u03b8 - p )(2b cos \u03b8 - p ) ]\n\nSimilarly, d - b = -(b - d )\n\nTherefore, the absolute values:\n\n|c - a | = p\u00b2 |b - d | / [ (2d cos \u03b8 - p )(2b cos \u03b8 - p ) ]\n\n|d - b | = |b - d | = |d - b |\n\nTherefore, OC\u00b7OA\u00b7BD = c a |d - b | = [ (p d )/(2d cos \u03b8 - p ) ] [ (p b )/(2b cos \u03b8 - p ) ] |d - b |\n\n= p\u00b2 b d |d - b | / [ (2d cos \u03b8 - p )(2b cos \u03b8 - p ) ]\n\nOB\u00b7OD\u00b7AC = b d |c - a | = b d [ p\u00b2 |b - d | / ( (2d cos \u03b8 - p )(2b cos \u03b8 - p ) ) ]\n\n= p\u00b2 b d |b - d | / [ (2d cos \u03b8 - p )(2b cos \u03b8 - p ) ]\n\nSince |d - b | = |b - d |, we have:\n\nOC\u00b7OA\u00b7BD = p\u00b2 b d |d - b | / denominator\n\nOB\u00b7OD\u00b7AC = p\u00b2 b d |d - b | / denominator\n\nTherefore, OC\u00b7OA\u00b7BD = OB\u00b7OD\u00b7AC\n\nHence, proved.\n\n**Final Answer**\n\\boxed{OC \\cdot OA \\cdot BD = OB \\cdot OD \\cdot AC}", "deepseek_solution": "Given an angle \\( \\angle XOY \\) with its bisector passing through point \\( P \\). Lines \\( AB \\) and \\( CD \\) pass through \\( P \\), intersecting \\( OX \\) at \\( A, C \\) and \\( OY \\) at \\( B, D \\) respectively. We need to prove that \\( OC \\cdot OA \\cdot BD = OB \\cdot OD \\cdot AC \\).\n\n1. **Coordinate Setup**:\n   - Place \\( O \\) at the origin.\n   - The angle bisector is the x-axis, with \\( OX \\) making an angle \\( \\theta \\) above the x-axis and \\( OY \\) making an angle \\( -\\theta \\) below the x-axis.\n   - Points \\( A \\) and \\( C \\) on \\( OX \\) have coordinates \\( (a \\cos \\theta, a \\sin \\theta) \\) and \\( (c \\cos \\theta, c \\sin \\theta) \\).\n   - Points \\( B \\) and \\( D \\) on \\( OY \\) have coordinates \\( (b \\cos \\theta, -b \\sin \\theta) \\) and \\( (d \\cos \\theta, -d \\sin \\theta) \\).\n   - Point \\( P \\) is on the x-axis at \\( (p, 0) \\).\n\n2. **Equations of Lines**:\n   - For line \\( AB \\) passing through \\( P \\), the parametric equations lead to the relation \\( p = \\frac{2ab \\cos \\theta}{a + b} \\).\n   - Similarly, for line \\( CD \\), we get \\( p = \\frac{2cd \\cos \\theta}{c + d} \\).\n\n3. **Expressing Coordinates**:\n   - Solving for \\( a \\) and \\( c \\) in terms of \\( b \\) and \\( d \\):\n     \\[\n     a = \\frac{pb}{2b \\cos \\theta - p}, \\quad c = \\frac{pd}{2d \\cos \\theta - p}\n     \\]\n\n4. **Distances Calculation**:\n   - \\( OA = a \\), \\( OB = b \\), \\( OC = c \\), \\( OD = d \\).\n   - \\( BD = |d - b| \\sqrt{\\cos^2 \\theta + \\sin^2 \\theta} = |d - b| \\).\n   - \\( AC = |c - a| \\sqrt{\\cos^2 \\theta + \\sin^2 \\theta} = |c - a| \\).\n\n5. **Verification**:\n   - Calculate \\( OC \\cdot OA \\cdot BD \\) and \\( OB \\cdot OD \\cdot AC \\):\n     \\[\n     OC \\cdot OA \\cdot BD = c \\cdot a \\cdot |d - b|\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     OB \\cdot OD \\cdot AC = b \\cdot d \\cdot |c - a|\n     \\]\n   - Substitute \\( a \\) and \\( c \\):\n     \\[\n     c - a = \\frac{p^2 (b - d)}{(2d \\cos \\theta - p)(2b \\cos \\theta - p)}\n     \\]\n   - Simplify and compare:\n     \\[\n     OC \\cdot OA \\cdot BD = \\frac{p^2 b d |d - b|}{(2d \\cos \\theta - p)(2b \\cos \\theta - p)} = OB \\cdot OD \\cdot AC\n     \\]\n\nThus, we have shown that \\( OC \\cdot OA \\cdot BD = OB \\cdot OD \\cdot AC \\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{OC \\cdot OA \\cdot BD = OB \\cdot OD \\cdot AC}\n\\]", "ground_truth_solution": "### Problem:\n\u8bbe $\\angle XOY$ \u7684\u5e73\u5206\u7ebf\u4e0a\u4efb\u610f\u4e00\u70b9\u4e3a $P$, \u8fc7 $P$ \u4f5c\u4e24\u6761\u4efb\u610f\u76f4\u7ebf $AB, CD$, \u5206\u522b\u4ea4 $OX, OY$ \u4e8e $A, C, B, D$. \u6c42\u8bc1: $OC \\cdot OA \\cdot BD = OB \\cdot OD \\cdot AC$.\n\n1. \u4ee4 $\\angle POA = \\angle POB = \\alpha$\u3002\u56e0\u4e3a $P$ \u5728 $\\angle XOY$ \u7684\u5e73\u5206\u7ebf\u4e0a\uff0c\u6240\u4ee5 $\\angle POA$ \u548c $\\angle POB$ \u76f8\u7b49\u3002\n\n2. \u4ee5 $O$ \u4e3a\u89c6\u70b9\uff0c\u5206\u522b\u5bf9 $B, P, A$ \u53ca $D, P, C$ \u4e09\u70b9\uff0c\u5e94\u7528\u5f20\u89d2\u5b9a\u7406\u7684\u63a8\u8bba\u3002\u5f20\u89d2\u5b9a\u7406\u544a\u8bc9\u6211\u4eec\uff0c\u5bf9\u4e8e\u67d0\u4e2a\u89d2\u7684\u5e73\u5206\u7ebf\u4e0a\u7684\u70b9 $P$\uff0c\u6ee1\u8db3\u4ee5\u4e0b\u5173\u7cfb\u5f0f\uff1a\n\n\\[\n\\cos \\alpha = \\frac{1}{2} \\left( \\frac{1}{OA} + \\frac{1}{OB} \\right) OP\n\\]\n\n\u5e94\u7528\u6b64\u5b9a\u7406\uff0c\u53ef\u4ee5\u5f97\u5230\u4ee5\u4e0b\u4e24\u4e2a\u5173\u7cfb\u5f0f\uff1